+# Changes, round 2
+
+Reworked `src/statement.mjs` against GAPS.md. All figures checked against `data/usage.json`.
+
+## Gaps closed
+
+1. Order by amount: charges run largest first, ties by service name A-Z (Compute 1,642.50, Managed database 1,296.00, Dedicated support 500.00, Data transfer out 394.20, Object storage 209.76, Container registry 41.20, Key management 36.00, Load balancing 36.00). Credits run largest first: Committed-use discount, then Service credit, 14 Sep outage.
+2. Charges subtotal: a rule under the last charge row, then a "Charges" row with 4,155.66 (and 100.0%) in the amount column, then the Credits block, then the rule and Total due. 4,155.66 less 574.88 of credits gives 3,580.78.
+3. Credits in parentheses with no minus sign: (410.63), (164.25). The decimal points stay in the amount column and the closing parenthesis hangs one column to the right. Credits have no rule under their heading.
+4. Zero-usage services are out of the table. A wrapped sentence under Total due says "2 services had no usage this month and are not listed: Machine learning inference, Monitoring." It is left out if none, and the wording handles one service.
+5. Share column, left of Amount: 39.5%, 31.2%, 12.0%, 9.5%, 5.0%, 1.0%, 0.9%, 0.9%, computed in integer arithmetic against the 4,155.66 subtotal, rounded half up to one decimal. The Charges row shows 100.0%. Credits and Total due have none.
+- Minor: the account number is flush right on line 1 beside the customer name. Quantity and unit are one left-aligned "Usage" column ("18,250 vCPU-hours").
+
+## Kept as before
+
+Month in words, commas, aligned decimals, "USD" only in the column heading, no "$", total last under a rule. Widest line is 61 characters (credit lines), limit 72. No tabs, no trailing spaces, ASCII only.
+
+## Left on purpose
+
+- Table width shrank from 69 to 60 columns. Credit labels may run across the empty Usage and Share columns, so only charge labels set the width. The cap of 72 is still enforced.
+- A service is dropped from the table only if both its quantity and its amount are zero. A zero-quantity line with a charge would still be shown, so nothing billed is hidden. A zero-usage service never changes the totals.
+- Wording ("Service", "Usage", "Share", "Total due", the closing sentence) follows GAPS.md and my reading of STYLE.md. I cannot compare it with the billing team's statement.
